         "title": "Katherine Vaz: “My father was on his deathbed when I was writing. He said ‘please finish it’. He thought it was a big book”",
         "description": "<p><span>In this conversation on “The Heart & Hustle of Portugal” podcast, hosted by Tony Gonçalves, the New York-based author Katherine Vaz recalled how her first novel, published by a major New York house, was advised against using the word “saudade” in its title. She insisted, and the word found its readers</span></p>",
